{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:d3c5e9a0bac78f84","name":"Grappler Mag","source":{"id":"source:reference-d3c5e9a0bac78f84","title":"Grappler Mag","revision":19672,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:23:38Z","sha256":"d13bbe302d122fa7b5fe685385e0f7bdf5765a9ed2f7f4dff510b913980df9f0","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19672","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Grappler%20Mag&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-d3c5e9a0bac78f84","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Emplacement Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Emplacement_Points"},":"]}," 1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 1,000\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A Grappler Mag is essentially a short-range ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"}," grappling hook with a magnetic clamp at the end. Designed before ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tractor Beam"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tractor_Beam","referenceId":"reference:627f44a03c76e65b"}," technology was widespread, Grapple Mags have been almost entirely surpassed by superior ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tractor Beams"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tractor_Beams"},". A Grappler Mag is treated as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tractor Beam"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tractor_Beam","referenceId":"reference:627f44a03c76e65b"}," with a range of 1. Though substantially limited when compared to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tractor Beams"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tractor_Beams"},", Grappler Mags can be fit on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," with far less difficulty.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The sole other advantage of a Grappler Mag is that it can be activated and maintained without the use of power, allowing ships equipped with it to appear dead while being attached to another ship. (All ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," have ordinary ",{"tag":"a","children":["Docking Clamps"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Docking_Clamps","referenceId":"reference:b4a9e9f91fcb2a40"}," for this purpose, but these clamps can be used to attach only to a willing or disabled ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"},".) As such, a smaller ship can use it clandestinely to attach to a vessel at least one size larger, without any telltale energy signatures to give away the smaller ship, but this requires the smaller vessel to make a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," check and a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stealth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stealth","referenceId":"reference:526a40a447ddd7aa"}," check opposed by the target ship's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," check and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check, respectively. If either of the smaller ship's checks is bested by the target ship's opposed ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Check"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Check"},", the smaller ship is detected while grappling itself to the hull.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
